"""Application factory for {{ project_name }}.

The canonical household shape:
  - lifespan chains the db engine and the FastMCP lifespan
  - /mcp is mounted as an ASGI sub-app (FastMCP HTTP transport), wrapped in the
    household's canonical Authentik bearer-token gate
  - The SPA is served from /frontend/build/ by app.frontend

The app exposes two surfaces and each is gated on its own terms — they are NOT
interchangeable (rules-library/platform/canonical-app-shape.md):

  - The HUMAN surface (/api, the SPA) is Tier 1a (Authentik proxy-delegated).
    Identity arrives in X-authentik-uid / X-authentik-username headers; no
    app-level sessions. See deps.py.
  - The MACHINE surface (/mcp) validates a live Authentik OIDC Bearer token
    app-side and resolves it against an actors.yaml allow-list. It does NOT
    trust a forwarded identity header: a machine caller does not traverse the
    human proxy, so header trust there would be a bypass. See mcp/http_auth.py.
    An app that is itself an authority for machine identity gates it through
    `app_hooks.mcp_auth` instead; everything else here is unchanged.
"""

